<title>USA: Concord Energy sell gas treatment plant.</title>
<headline>Concord Energy sell gas treatment plant.</headline>
<dateline>JOURDANTON, Texas 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Concord Energy Inc said Tuesday it sold a 1,200 gallons per minute amine gas treatment plant to the Royal Dutch/Shell Group's Shell Oil Co for $8 million, including installation.</p>
<p>Concord said it expects to complete the project within 120 days.</p>
<p>&quot;This contract represents a significant increase in our estimated fiscal 1998 revenues,&quot; Concord said, noting this is the single largest contract ever executed by its Kemco subsidiary.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
